# Audio that a script writes. All of it was tracked for a while, and since
# mixdown.sh rewrites these files on every run, each rebuild added another
# forty five megabytes to the history: 1,451 MB across fifty nine blobs of
# build output, in a repository whose source is fourteen.
#
# Everything ignored here regenerates: speak.py writes the narration, score.py
# writes the Lyria pieces from fixed seeds, mixdown.sh writes the rest.
# audio/sfx is deliberately not ignored, because those came from Mixkit and
# nothing in this tree can produce them again.
audio/build/
audio/vo/
audio/score/
audio/voices/
audio/bed.wav
